			<item>
				<title>The $139,258 check</title>
				<link>https://emesshalom18.github.io/emesvshalom-site/financial-overview/check-139258/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://emesshalom18.github.io/emesvshalom-site/financial-overview/check-139258/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;This check is presented as evidence against the claim that the Ort family&#xA;was left with nothing.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &#xA;&#xA;&lt;img src=&#34;https://emesshalom18.github.io/emesvshalom-site/evidence/checks/ort-real-estate-account/2010-02-16/display/check-139258.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Check #1057 for $139,258.00&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What the document shows:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Drawer: Philip Ort Real Estate Account, Brooklyn NY&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Check #1057, dated 2/16/10&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Payee: Manya Ort&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Amount: $139,258.00&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Handwritten note on the face: &lt;em&gt;&amp;ldquo;Accepted as payment IN FULL for all monies&#xA;outstanding to all Ort Children without RESERVATION. If that&amp;rsquo;s not&#xA;acceptable, DON&amp;rsquo;T DEPOSIT THIS CHECK. I&amp;rsquo;m NOT going to go through all these&#xA;figures AGAIN, under ANY CIRCUMSTANCE.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What it does and doesn&amp;rsquo;t prove.&lt;/strong&gt; The check documents a $139,258 payment&#xA;from the real-estate account to Mrs. Ort in February 2010. The handwritten&#xA;note frames it as a conditional full settlement of outstanding child-related&#xA;monies — conditional because it instructs the recipient not to deposit it if&#xA;the &amp;ldquo;in full&amp;rdquo; characterization is not accepted. Whether it settled the&#xA;claims is a question for the underlying dispute; the scan alone records the&#xA;offer and the condition.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
